PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
- Consensus Status: Unanimous agreement across all 15 participants on Option B (mademoiselle).
- Choreographic Analysis: The opening verse divides into two distinct thematic couplets. Mia Wallace exaggerates her right leg on the cadence downbeats of the first couplet ("well" and "mademoiselle"), before shifting her focus to the left leg for the second couplet ("bell" and "tell").
- Conclusion: Competing options are excluded as either the first right-leg accent ("well"), fluid mid-phrase transitions ("truly"), or left-leg movements post-transition. The answer remains definitively B. mademoiselle.
}

